phi'' - V'(phi) = 0
first-order (Bogomolny) equation phi' = sqrt(2 V(phi)) = (sqrt(lam/2)) (v^2 - phi^2): True
energy density = phi'^2 (gradient and potential energies are equal): True
E = 2/3*sqrt(2)*sqrt(lam)*v^3   equals (2 sqrt 2/3) sqrt(lam) v^3: True
the kink interpolates between the vacua: limits -v and v
